# Angin

A small React component library with native form props, composable layout,
explicit styling, and CommonJS/ES module builds. React is provided by your app;
Angin has no other runtime dependencies.

```sh
npm install angin react react-dom
```

```tsx
import { Button, Input, Stack } from 'angin';
import 'angin/styles.css';

export function ContactForm() {
    return (
        <form className="angin-root">
            <Stack gap="md">
                <Input id="contact-email" name="email" label="Email" type="email" required />
                <Button type="submit">Subscribe</Button>
            </Stack>
        </form>
    );
}
```

Use unique explicit IDs when server rendering. Import CSS once in your app's
entry point; `.angin-root` applies typography, box sizing, and native control
font inheritance. Components also work within your own layout.

